# Plain TAN CTYPEs with SIP keywords where one coefficient is written with a
# zero-padded index, A_01_1 (synthetic, from the round-2 verifier probe
# zz_sip_leading_zero).
# wcslib 8.10 ACCEPTS this header: its keyword lexer (wcspih.l,
# <SIP2>{Z1}_{Z1}"   ") takes single-digit indices only and DISCARDS the
# A_01_1 card without a message, so the polynomial loses that term; astropy
# 8.0.2 ignores it too. A_01_1 is not a SIP keyword, but it plainly means a
# coefficient, so dropping it would be silent data loss and applying it as
# A_1_1 would differ from wcslib. We refuse it (rule 7). AP/BP are given so
# hdr2sky injects nothing.
# EXPECT-GO-ERROR: A_01_1 is not a SIP coefficient keyword
NOTE stricter: sip_index_leading_zero
GRID 1 1024 5 1 1024 5
HEADER
NAXIS   = 2
NAXIS1  = 1024
NAXIS2  = 1024
CRVAL1  = 150.0
CRVAL2  = 2.0
CRPIX1  = 512.5
CRPIX2  = 512.5
CTYPE1  = 'RA---TAN'
CTYPE2  = 'DEC--TAN'
CD1_1   = -0.0002777
CD1_2   = 0.0
CD2_1   = 0.0
CD2_2   = 0.0002777
A_ORDER = 2
B_ORDER = 2
A_2_0   = 2e-5
A_01_1  = 1e-5
B_0_2   = 2e-5
B_1_1   = -1e-5
AP_ORDER= 1
AP_0_0  = 0.0
BP_ORDER= 1
BP_0_0  = 0.0
